    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4284",
      "problem": "Given the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ shown below, draw the linear combination $2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251898/assets/325e4a450d89ee1f5db4afd237dbc7d58efafec72d080386788f0491cc35950b.png)",
      "worked_solution": "- The vector $2\\mathbf{a}$ has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$ but twice the magnitude.\n\n- Likewise, the vector $3\\mathbf{b}$ has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$ but three times the magnitude.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251898/assets/066784522a39671fe57b157c6c692f5c56295126b8ec6f150d917e783ab63400.png)\n\nNow, we can draw $3\\mathbf{b}$ starting from the head of $2\\mathbf{a}.$ The resultant \n\n$$\n2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\ngoes from the tail of $2\\mathbf{a}$ to the head of $3\\mathbf{b}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251898/assets/d1dd084ad4f8f717afac515471bcba679fbe545f266435a57fb1c94d0d5c9cca.png)",
